# The kit's Verus files: the kit/templates paths kit/sync.sh copies to
# verus/make/templates/ (each as NAME.tmpl, so that no vendored path ends
# in a file name the port's code owners protect, such as
# reviewers.yaml), and so the files `make verus-headers`
# (headers.sh) holds a port's to, one a line; an installed port's are
# read from the package's templates/ under these names. Each holds its
# header, the leading `#` lines up to a `# kit: proved-port` line where
# it has one (a vendored port's file must; an installed port's need not,
# and its header is then its whole leading comment), but
# .chainguard/review-prompt.md, which holds its vendored-kit rule (the
# `- The vendored kit` item). The kit's other templates (conformance,
# consumers, fuzz, test, lint, the environments, develop.yaml,
# deps.yaml) are starting points the port reshapes, and are not held.
verus/FLOOR
verus/RLIMIT
verus/REACH
verus/MINTS
verus/count.toml
.chainguard/ci/verus.yaml
.chainguard/ci/miri.yaml
.chainguard/reviewers.yaml
.chainguard/review-prompt.md
